1
00:00:01,290 --> 00:00:03,170
How?

2
00:00:04,480 --> 00:00:06,810
How could I have forgotten?

3
00:00:06,810 --> 00:00:09,190
I made such an important promise...

4
00:00:09,190 --> 00:00:12,870
Compete with mathematicians
from all over Japan.

5
00:00:12,870 --> 00:00:14,710
I will solve your equation.

6
00:00:14,710 --> 00:00:17,720
I will answer whatever question you give me.

7
00:00:17,720 --> 00:00:19,410
It is a promise.

8
00:00:20,770 --> 00:00:23,570
Mathematics will always tie us together.

9
00:00:23,570 --> 00:00:26,360
Promise? What promise?

10
00:00:26,360 --> 00:00:29,670
Ikuru, sorry. I have to go.

11
00:00:29,670 --> 00:00:31,380
Wait!

12
00:00:33,480 --> 00:00:35,840
Why would you try to go alone?

13
00:00:35,840 --> 00:00:39,050
Ms. Nashiki, you know nothing
about this modern era.

14
00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:44,530
Why do you think I'm here for you?

15
00:00:51,240 --> 00:00:52,740
I'm so sorry!

16
00:00:52,740 --> 00:00:55,380
My hands, they just...

17
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:01,430
Ikuru.

18
00:01:02,040 --> 00:01:04,110
Will you take me there?

19
00:01:04,110 --> 00:01:05,600
Where?

20
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:09,610
The Konno Hachimangu Shrine,
in Shibuya Village.

21
00:01:11,380 --> 00:01:12,870
That's so local.

22
00:01:18,890 --> 00:01:20,510
Here we are.

23
00:01:22,860 --> 00:01:27,830
This is... the Konno Hachimangu Shrine.

24
00:01:33,810 --> 00:01:39,870
[Konno Hachimangu Shrine]

25
00:01:51,670 --> 00:01:54,750
The shrine, it wasn't like this at all.

26
00:01:54,750 --> 00:01:57,300
The locale is still called Shibuya,

27
00:01:57,300 --> 00:01:59,280
so this must be the place.

28
00:01:59,280 --> 00:02:00,690
But I don't see the plaques!

29
00:02:00,690 --> 00:02:02,390
The plaques?

30
00:02:04,710 --> 00:02:06,740
They're over there.

31
00:02:12,290 --> 00:02:14,870
No, not plaques like this.

32
00:02:14,870 --> 00:02:16,200
A mathematics plaque!

33
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:18,100
A mathematics plaque?

34
00:02:18,100 --> 00:02:21,540
You mean those plaques
they'd pose a question on,

35
00:02:21,540 --> 00:02:24,200
- in hopes someone would solve it?
- Yes, those plaques.

36
00:02:24,200 --> 00:02:28,810
There was a slew of questions
displayed here!

37
00:02:28,810 --> 00:02:32,570
<i>The hardest questions were challenged
by mathematicians from all across Japan.</i>

38
00:02:32,570 --> 00:02:34,980
I see.

39
00:02:34,980 --> 00:02:37,780
Should we check in there?

40
00:02:37,780 --> 00:02:40,430
Please don't run ahead!

41
00:02:41,610 --> 00:02:43,390
[Museum]

42
00:02:57,060 --> 00:03:00,480
Ms. Nashiki, I think I found it!

43
00:03:06,150 --> 00:03:08,250
[Seki]

44
00:03:09,340 --> 00:03:11,250
Master Seki...

45
00:03:16,140 --> 00:03:19,940
Looks old. I wonder when it's from.

46
00:03:19,940 --> 00:03:21,180
Jokyo 2.

47
00:03:21,180 --> 00:03:24,860
That's when Master Seki was studying circles.

48
00:03:24,860 --> 00:03:29,140
Right. He discovered pi in Japan, didn't he?

49
00:03:29,140 --> 00:03:33,340
If the country weren't closed off,
he'd be on par with Newton.

50
00:03:33,340 --> 00:03:36,610
At least, that's what all our textbooks say.

51
00:03:38,880 --> 00:03:43,230
Master Seki was indeed a genius.

52
00:03:43,230 --> 00:03:47,000
He worked tirelessly for the Kofu Domain.

53
00:03:47,720 --> 00:03:50,890
I see. So he became a direct retainer
to the shogunate later.

54
00:03:50,890 --> 00:03:53,800
What? A direct retainer?

55
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:55,490
- Yes.
- To the shogunate?

56
00:03:55,490 --> 00:03:58,960
Yes. It says he was promoted later in life.

57
00:04:00,540 --> 00:04:02,400
Master Seki...

58
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:06,130
So you became a retainer to the shogun.

59
00:04:06,840 --> 00:04:10,090
That's amazing.

60
00:04:10,090 --> 00:04:13,580
Of course, I knew that already.

61
00:04:14,780 --> 00:04:18,410
But to think you were so far out of reach.

62
00:04:48,860 --> 00:04:51,910
I wonder why I'm here at all.

63
00:04:54,060 --> 00:04:57,200
It really was so sudden.

64
00:04:57,200 --> 00:05:00,170
I'm still confused by it all.

65
00:05:01,800 --> 00:05:04,030
Do you dislike this world?

66
00:05:05,840 --> 00:05:08,410
I think this place is wonderful.

67
00:05:11,550 --> 00:05:14,510
Nights are bright.

68
00:05:14,510 --> 00:05:16,590
Anyone can follow their dreams.

69
00:05:16,590 --> 00:05:19,340
Even young women like myself
can become teachers.

70
00:05:20,560 --> 00:05:25,800
But this isn't where I belong.

71
00:05:27,820 --> 00:05:32,280
Is that because Master Seki isn't here?

72
00:05:35,930 --> 00:05:39,680
How is that any different
from the world you came from?

73
00:05:39,680 --> 00:05:42,250
If he became a retainer,
you wouldn't see him anyway.

74
00:05:42,250 --> 00:05:44,300
You think I don't know that?

75
00:05:44,300 --> 00:05:48,860
Given my standing,
I have no right speaking to him.

76
00:05:48,860 --> 00:05:51,420
- Even so...
- Don't get so ahead of yourself.

77
00:05:51,420 --> 00:05:55,710
He's probably forgotten the daughter
of a commoner already.

78
00:05:55,710 --> 00:05:58,490
He left me a plaque to solve.

79
00:05:58,490 --> 00:06:01,040
He left it to the shrine.

80
00:06:01,040 --> 00:06:05,580
He put it up on display, for all to solve!

81
00:06:05,580 --> 00:06:07,600
Enough!

82
00:06:11,200 --> 00:06:14,600
Master Seki and I resided under the same sky.

83
00:06:14,600 --> 00:06:16,500
<i>That was...</i>

84
00:06:16,500 --> 00:06:19,960
That was enough for me.

85
00:06:20,880 --> 00:06:23,140
You wouldn't understand, Ikuru.

86
00:06:27,030 --> 00:06:29,410
Then just leave!

87
00:06:29,410 --> 00:06:31,910
If you can go home, then go!

88
00:06:31,910 --> 00:06:36,170
Do you think I'm looking after you
because I want to?

89
00:06:38,670 --> 00:06:40,890
<i>I just happened to be there when it happened.</i>

90
00:06:40,890 --> 00:06:42,770
<i>That's it.</i>

91
00:06:44,060 --> 00:06:46,590
If I could, I would've abandoned you already.

92
00:06:46,590 --> 00:06:48,810
I'm busy enough as is.

93
00:07:14,420 --> 00:07:17,550
[Episode 4]

94
00:07:21,730 --> 00:07:23,570
- I'm home.
- Welcome back!

95
00:07:23,570 --> 00:07:25,830
Look, I tried making omurice today!

96
00:07:25,830 --> 00:07:27,830
You wanted me to cook, right?

97
00:07:27,830 --> 00:07:30,220
See? It looks adorable!

98
00:07:30,990 --> 00:07:33,250
Huh? Where's Iroha?

99
00:07:33,250 --> 00:07:34,390
Dunno.

100
00:07:34,390 --> 00:07:36,160
What? Why?

101
00:07:36,160 --> 00:07:38,110
Didn't you two come home together?

102
00:07:38,110 --> 00:07:39,750
Hey!

103
00:07:46,940 --> 00:07:50,000
<i>Why am I so irritated?</i>

104
00:07:51,720 --> 00:07:52,630
This is awful...

105
00:07:52,630 --> 00:07:54,120
What the hell?

106
00:07:54,120 --> 00:07:56,310
This is awesome!

107
00:07:56,310 --> 00:07:59,980
Like cherry blossom colored snowflakes!

108
00:07:59,980 --> 00:08:04,400
<i>I'm better off without a crazy girl like her.</i>

109
00:08:07,050 --> 00:08:08,790
Ikuru.

110
00:08:10,370 --> 00:08:12,510
Why isn't Iroha coming back?

111
00:08:12,510 --> 00:08:14,690
Her phone's turned off.

112
00:08:14,690 --> 00:08:17,360
Maybe she doesn't know how to turn it on?

113
00:08:17,360 --> 00:08:22,000
And now she's lost,
and can't find her way back...

114
00:08:22,830 --> 00:08:26,190
Ikuru, what if something happens to her?

115
00:08:26,190 --> 00:08:27,480
So what if something happens?

116
00:08:27,480 --> 00:08:30,500
She's free to leave as suddenly as she came.

117
00:08:30,500 --> 00:08:32,260
But then...

118
00:08:32,260 --> 00:08:34,320
We'd never see her again.

119
00:08:34,320 --> 00:08:36,340
Just pretend she never existed
in the first place.

120
00:08:36,340 --> 00:08:39,870
It's not like she was
supposed to be here anyway.

121
00:08:39,870 --> 00:08:43,330
You're such a jerk! Stupid Ikuru!

122
00:09:32,350 --> 00:09:34,670
- Yikes!
- Run!

123
00:09:34,670 --> 00:09:36,970
- Hurry!
- Hey, wait!

124
00:09:36,970 --> 00:09:38,860
Why are you running?

125
00:09:41,560 --> 00:09:44,010
Ms. Nashiki?

126
00:09:44,010 --> 00:09:45,280
Huh?

127
00:09:46,330 --> 00:09:48,700
Are you a kid from school?

128
00:09:49,300 --> 00:09:53,160
I'm Naoya Sano. A third grader in Class 1.

129
00:09:53,160 --> 00:09:56,510
One of Mr. Majima's kids?

130
00:09:56,510 --> 00:09:58,380
What're you doing out so late?

131
00:09:58,380 --> 00:10:02,000
Ms. Nashiki, will you tell the school?

132
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:03,650
About?

133
00:10:09,830 --> 00:10:12,910
So you all were painting pictures.

134
00:10:13,620 --> 00:10:15,570
Everyone's so talented.

135
00:10:15,570 --> 00:10:17,070
Great colors, too.

136
00:10:17,070 --> 00:10:20,230
I knew it. You're the best, Ms. Nashiki!

137
00:10:20,230 --> 00:10:22,550
Do you live close by?

138
00:10:22,550 --> 00:10:25,110
I'll walk you home.

139
00:10:25,110 --> 00:10:26,280
I can walk home alone.

140
00:10:26,280 --> 00:10:28,350
Now don't say that.

141
00:10:28,350 --> 00:10:33,380
Even in my Edo era,
we don't let kids walk alone at night.

142
00:10:33,380 --> 00:10:36,120
I don't get what you're saying,

143
00:10:36,120 --> 00:10:38,820
but you're so weird, Ms. Nashiki.

144
00:10:39,740 --> 00:10:42,180
Class 3 is so lucky.

145
00:10:42,180 --> 00:10:45,180
I wish I was in your class, too.

146
00:10:46,780 --> 00:10:48,780
I appreciate the thought, Naoya.

147
00:10:49,830 --> 00:10:52,470
But there's still so much I don't know.

148
00:10:53,670 --> 00:10:56,360
Including where I'm supposed to belong.

149
00:10:58,140 --> 00:10:59,470
Come on, let's go.

150
00:10:59,470 --> 00:11:01,690
- This way.
- Alright.

151
00:11:01,690 --> 00:11:04,450
Hey, wait up!

152
00:11:15,930 --> 00:11:18,280
This is where you live?

153
00:11:18,280 --> 00:11:20,740
Yeah. On the second floor.

154
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:24,070
Naoya.

155
00:11:24,070 --> 00:11:25,360
- Welcome home.
- I'm back.

156
00:11:25,360 --> 00:11:27,330
- Hey there, kiddo.
- Welcome home.

157
00:11:30,830 --> 00:11:34,340
Ms. Nashiki, come on in.

158
00:11:34,340 --> 00:11:35,750
Sure.

159
00:11:42,470 --> 00:11:44,190
What's wrong?

160
00:11:46,480 --> 00:11:50,810
Nothing's wrong. This just takes me back.

161
00:11:52,750 --> 00:11:54,300
How's that?

162
00:11:56,170 --> 00:11:58,110
- We're back!
- Welcome back.

163
00:11:58,110 --> 00:11:59,980
You're as quick as ever.

164
00:11:59,980 --> 00:12:03,010
We helped put out a fire along the way.

165
00:12:03,010 --> 00:12:05,270
Is that so? Great job helping out.

166
00:12:05,270 --> 00:12:06,510
Anyone hungry?

167
00:12:06,510 --> 00:12:08,300
- Me!
- Alright.

168
00:12:13,150 --> 00:12:17,750
They want to show off their skin so bad,
it's almost funny.

169
00:12:20,300 --> 00:12:22,810
Ms. Nashiki. This way.

170
00:12:33,680 --> 00:12:35,390
Come on in.

171
00:12:35,390 --> 00:12:37,090
Thanks for having me.

172
00:13:04,880 --> 00:13:08,000
What's this? A carrier case?

173
00:13:08,980 --> 00:13:10,810
- Somehow, it's...
- No touching, Ms. Nashiki!

174
00:13:10,810 --> 00:13:12,780
Right, sorry.

175
00:13:13,680 --> 00:13:15,250
That's Dad's work.

176
00:13:15,250 --> 00:13:17,550
I help out a bit, too.

177
00:13:17,550 --> 00:13:19,730
I see.

178
00:13:19,730 --> 00:13:22,070
Have a seat.

179
00:13:22,070 --> 00:13:25,400
- Are you hungry?
- Nah, I'm fine.

180
00:13:25,400 --> 00:13:26,790
What about you?

181
00:13:26,790 --> 00:13:29,140
Let's see...

182
00:13:31,470 --> 00:13:35,840
There's still rice! Awesome!

183
00:13:35,840 --> 00:13:38,620
Which means...

184
00:13:38,620 --> 00:13:41,370
Look, we have eggs.

185
00:13:41,370 --> 00:13:43,680
I can make Dad's favorite.

186
00:13:43,680 --> 00:13:45,290
And what's that?

187
00:13:45,290 --> 00:13:47,440
Egg on rice!

188
00:13:49,200 --> 00:13:51,410
Eggs sure are tasty, aren't they?

189
00:13:51,410 --> 00:13:52,920
Yeah!

190
00:13:56,930 --> 00:13:59,700
Naoya, where's your Mom?

191
00:13:59,700 --> 00:14:01,150
She's not here.

192
00:14:01,150 --> 00:14:03,660
Dad says she ran away.

193
00:14:03,660 --> 00:14:05,240
Ran away?

194
00:14:05,240 --> 00:14:07,790
She found someone else.

195
00:14:07,790 --> 00:14:10,240
Someone she liked more than me and Dad.

196
00:14:12,410 --> 00:14:14,750
What?

197
00:14:14,750 --> 00:14:17,620
Hey, you have miso, too.

198
00:14:17,620 --> 00:14:20,250
- This is miso, right?
- Yup.

199
00:14:26,780 --> 00:14:29,080
Want me to crack that egg?

200
00:14:29,080 --> 00:14:31,380
- Nope.
- Alright, give it a shot.

201
00:14:33,160 --> 00:14:36,810
Hey, you're good!

202
00:14:36,810 --> 00:14:39,550
- Naoya.
- Dad!

203
00:14:39,550 --> 00:14:42,210
- Welcome home!
- Thanks.

204
00:14:44,630 --> 00:14:46,080
Who's this?

205
00:14:48,530 --> 00:14:50,440
Master Seki?

206
00:14:50,440 --> 00:14:53,330
This is Ms. Nashiki. She teaches Class 3!

207
00:14:53,330 --> 00:14:55,610
Ah, the teacher.

208
00:14:55,610 --> 00:14:58,810
Why're you here? Did Naoya cause trouble?

209
00:14:59,350 --> 00:15:01,230
No, he did nothing wrong.

210
00:15:01,230 --> 00:15:03,810
Ms. Nashiki, I'm putting in the egg.

211
00:15:03,810 --> 00:15:07,230
S-Sure. Be careful.

212
00:15:24,340 --> 00:15:26,210
Master Seki...

213
00:15:27,780 --> 00:15:29,320
Huh?

214
00:15:29,320 --> 00:15:31,940
It's me, Iroha.

215
00:15:32,760 --> 00:15:37,690
Thank goodness. You made it here, too.

216
00:15:37,690 --> 00:15:43,300
I... I wanted to see you.

217
00:15:44,140 --> 00:15:46,370
- Master Seki!
- Woah.

218
00:15:46,370 --> 00:15:47,970
Don't touch me.

219
00:15:49,220 --> 00:15:50,860
It spilled over!

220
00:15:50,860 --> 00:15:54,990
- Ms. Nashiki, the pot!
- Hold on.

221
00:15:57,170 --> 00:16:00,040
Bon appétit.

222
00:16:00,040 --> 00:16:02,600
- Bon appétit.
- Thanks for the meal.

223
00:16:07,450 --> 00:16:09,540
Hot!

224
00:16:14,440 --> 00:16:16,120
Yum.

225
00:16:19,420 --> 00:16:22,110
What? You're making it hard to eat.

226
00:16:25,950 --> 00:16:29,190
- Master Seki...
- Sorry, who is that?

227
00:16:31,500 --> 00:16:33,650
Do I look like someone you know?

228
00:16:35,520 --> 00:16:39,160
- Or are you flirting with me?
- "Flirting"?

229
00:16:39,160 --> 00:16:40,470
Dad, you know what?

230
00:16:40,470 --> 00:16:45,550
Ms. Nashiki's class seems so fun!

231
00:16:49,660 --> 00:16:51,430
You've got rice there.

232
00:16:52,020 --> 00:16:54,400
- Thanks.
- Sure.

233
00:16:57,150 --> 00:16:59,350
Ms. Nashiki.

234
00:16:59,350 --> 00:17:01,050
Can you help me with my homework later?

235
00:17:01,050 --> 00:17:04,000
Ms. Nashiki has to go home.

236
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:05,820
Well...

237
00:17:06,950 --> 00:17:10,180
If you wouldn't mind me staying...

238
00:17:10,180 --> 00:17:11,800
Yes!

239
00:17:11,800 --> 00:17:14,690
Oh, but dinner first.

240
00:17:52,670 --> 00:17:53,920
[3rd Grade Math]

241
00:18:06,250 --> 00:18:07,820
Excuse me.

242
00:18:09,230 --> 00:18:12,000
Are you really not Master Seki?

243
00:18:14,710 --> 00:18:16,510
You don't remember me at all?

244
00:18:16,510 --> 00:18:18,010
Knock it off.

245
00:18:18,760 --> 00:18:21,410
If you're done here, why don't you go home?

246
00:18:34,740 --> 00:18:37,030
What're you doing?

247
00:18:38,970 --> 00:18:40,420
Allow me to help.

248
00:18:40,420 --> 00:18:44,540
I once worked making paper umbrellas, see.

249
00:18:45,940 --> 00:18:47,610
Paper umbrellas?

250
00:18:54,040 --> 00:18:56,630
Then check to see
if there aren't any damages.

251
00:18:56,630 --> 00:18:58,620
Check?

252
00:18:59,540 --> 00:19:02,430
Then you fold the instructions like this,

253
00:19:03,110 --> 00:19:04,900
and put it in this package.

254
00:19:04,900 --> 00:19:06,680
Package...

255
00:19:06,680 --> 00:19:10,420
Make sure you put the sticker on straight.

256
00:19:12,940 --> 00:19:14,300
Here.

257
00:19:15,880 --> 00:19:17,220
Yes, sir.

258
00:19:33,330 --> 00:19:37,080
Say, what are these things?

259
00:19:37,720 --> 00:19:39,290
Magatama?
(T/N: Prehistoric beads)

260
00:19:39,290 --> 00:19:40,700
- Huh?
- What?

261
00:19:40,700 --> 00:19:42,710
- "Magatama"?
- Yes.

262
00:19:42,710 --> 00:19:44,100
- What're those?
- Huh?

263
00:19:44,100 --> 00:19:46,200
- Huh?
- You've never seen them?

264
00:19:47,590 --> 00:19:50,670
She'll at least come to school, right?

265
00:19:50,670 --> 00:19:54,150
Why did I make this my business...

266
00:20:03,800 --> 00:20:06,000
Wait, don't tell me it's...

267
00:20:11,880 --> 00:20:12,830
<i>Love!</i>

268
00:20:12,830 --> 00:20:15,000
No, no, no.

269
00:20:16,700 --> 00:20:19,240
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

270
00:20:19,240 --> 00:20:21,870
- Mr. Majima.
- I'll take that.

271
00:20:21,870 --> 00:20:24,180
- Thank you...
- Woah!

272
00:20:24,180 --> 00:20:27,230
- Are you alright?
- Yes. Sorry about that.

273
00:20:27,230 --> 00:20:29,400
Here, I've got it.

274
00:20:29,400 --> 00:20:30,450
Could you grab those?

275
00:20:30,450 --> 00:20:32,980
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

276
00:20:35,030 --> 00:20:36,670
- Hey.
- Woah!

277
00:20:36,670 --> 00:20:39,330
Don't scare me like that. Morning.

278
00:20:40,650 --> 00:20:42,770
You look terrible.

279
00:20:42,770 --> 00:20:44,480
Are you alright?

280
00:20:44,480 --> 00:20:46,030
And I reckon you managed to sleep.

281
00:20:46,030 --> 00:20:48,730
Huh? Oh, right.

282
00:20:48,730 --> 00:20:51,130
Yeah, I did sleep.

283
00:20:51,130 --> 00:20:53,230
Outside?

284
00:20:53,230 --> 00:20:56,020
No. Inside a home.

285
00:20:56,020 --> 00:20:57,650
Inside a home?

286
00:21:00,300 --> 00:21:02,550
Inside a home...

287
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:05,800
Whose home?

288
00:21:06,900 --> 00:21:09,190
Well...

289
00:21:09,190 --> 00:21:12,190
That is to say...

290
00:21:12,190 --> 00:21:15,330
Ow! Hot!

291
00:21:16,440 --> 00:21:18,410
Never mind.

292
00:21:19,160 --> 00:21:22,100
<i>Never mind?</i>

293
00:21:26,620 --> 00:21:31,400
<i>Who did Ms. Nashiki stay with last night?</i>

294
00:21:31,400 --> 00:21:34,940
Follow my lead, alright?

295
00:21:36,400 --> 00:21:39,700
You have to keep it speedy.

296
00:21:43,620 --> 00:21:45,590
Now you all give it a try.

297
00:21:45,590 --> 00:21:47,210
Ready?

298
00:21:48,310 --> 00:21:51,420
Next group. Ready?

299
00:21:51,420 --> 00:21:58,120
<i>No way. Did she stay over at Mr. Majima's?</i>

300
00:21:59,960 --> 00:22:02,440
<i>She stayed the night...</i>

301
00:22:02,440 --> 00:22:06,580
- <i>With him?</i>
- Careful, watch for your classmates.

302
00:22:06,580 --> 00:22:08,160
Ms. Akutsu.

303
00:22:12,830 --> 00:22:14,670
Isn't she the worst?

304
00:22:14,670 --> 00:22:16,910
She blocked me without any warning!

305
00:22:16,910 --> 00:22:19,710
The person from the dating app?
But you two went on a date.

306
00:22:19,710 --> 00:22:21,640
Where did I go wrong?

307
00:22:21,640 --> 00:22:24,430
I spent hours drafting my texts to her!

308
00:22:24,430 --> 00:22:25,440
That's it.

309
00:22:25,440 --> 00:22:28,070
Konishi, have you ever had a girlfriend?

310
00:22:28,070 --> 00:22:30,890
I'm working hard to change that!

311
00:22:32,400 --> 00:22:36,790
Just so you know, 46% of men
in their twenties have never dated before.

312
00:22:36,790 --> 00:22:38,540
Kamiya!

313
00:22:38,540 --> 00:22:39,660
My sole ally!

314
00:22:39,660 --> 00:22:41,740
Sorry, I have a girlfriend.

315
00:22:41,740 --> 00:22:43,320
What's gotten you so anxious?

316
00:22:43,320 --> 00:22:46,970
Choosing not to date
is a perfectly valid option.

317
00:22:47,750 --> 00:22:50,850
Any other chronically single people here?

318
00:22:52,560 --> 00:22:54,950
Just me, huh?

319
00:22:56,210 --> 00:22:59,790
<i>No, there's another right here.</i>

320
00:22:59,790 --> 00:23:03,400
<i>Ms. Nashiki already has Mr. Majima.</i>

321
00:23:03,400 --> 00:23:04,890
<i>She has Master Seki, too.</i>

322
00:23:04,890 --> 00:23:08,480
<i>But I lived under the same roof as her!</i>

323
00:23:09,080 --> 00:23:13,630
Look, Mr. Ichinose's so sad for you, Konishi.

324
00:23:13,630 --> 00:23:17,070
Yeah? Well, I want to cry, too!

325
00:23:17,070 --> 00:23:20,100
- Good afternoon.
- Afternoon.

326
00:23:20,100 --> 00:23:21,760
Mr. Majima.

327
00:23:23,030 --> 00:23:24,440
Listen...

328
00:23:26,110 --> 00:23:27,550
Could I have a minute?

329
00:23:33,070 --> 00:23:35,490
Naoya Sano?

330
00:23:35,980 --> 00:23:38,750
How do you know him?

331
00:23:38,750 --> 00:23:41,940
Let's just say we bumped into each other.

332
00:23:43,590 --> 00:23:44,850
I see.

333
00:23:45,600 --> 00:23:48,820
Did he tell you he wanted to join Class 3?

334
00:23:48,820 --> 00:23:50,490
Huh?

335
00:23:50,490 --> 00:23:52,270
Oh, no.

336
00:23:53,510 --> 00:24:00,110
I wanted to ask a question
about Naoya's father.

337
00:24:00,110 --> 00:24:02,920
What sort of individual is he?

338
00:24:02,920 --> 00:24:06,670
Actually, I haven't met him myself.

339
00:24:06,670 --> 00:24:07,560
What?

340
00:24:07,560 --> 00:24:10,070
I wasn't able to contact him
for our meeting in April,

341
00:24:10,070 --> 00:24:14,530
and I haven't gotten permission
to visit him at home either.

342
00:24:15,030 --> 00:24:18,540
Perhaps he's busy with work?

343
00:24:19,520 --> 00:24:24,190
Or he works an unusual schedule.

344
00:24:24,190 --> 00:24:26,810
Naoya often sleeps during class.

345
00:24:26,810 --> 00:24:30,530
That usually indicates an issue at home.

346
00:24:31,390 --> 00:24:34,320
I hope to meet with his father soon.

347
00:24:34,320 --> 00:24:36,590
I see.

348
00:24:36,590 --> 00:24:38,290
- Mr. Majima.
- Yes?

349
00:24:38,290 --> 00:24:40,390
Kizaki's parents have come.

350
00:24:40,390 --> 00:24:42,000
Would you please see to them?

351
00:24:42,000 --> 00:24:43,730
Her parents?

352
00:24:43,730 --> 00:24:45,830
[NextCore - Michio Kizaki]

353
00:24:47,130 --> 00:24:49,390
The President of NextCore?

354
00:24:49,390 --> 00:24:51,530
- Are you listening?
- Yes.

355
00:24:51,530 --> 00:24:55,270
My daughter had a bruise on her back.

356
00:24:55,270 --> 00:24:59,620
A bruise, on a young girl's back!

357
00:24:59,620 --> 00:25:04,300
As I hear, a child named Naoya Sano
went on a rampage during gym class.

358
00:25:05,370 --> 00:25:08,450
Did you even try to stop him?

359
00:25:08,450 --> 00:25:11,040
Yes, of course.

360
00:25:12,380 --> 00:25:14,370
<i>Are you okay?</i>

361
00:25:14,370 --> 00:25:17,040
<i>Knock it off, Sano.</i>

362
00:25:17,040 --> 00:25:21,390
Pardon me, but you are still quite young, no?

363
00:25:22,380 --> 00:25:25,770
I wouldn't be surprised
if you couldn't stop a mere child.

364
00:25:25,770 --> 00:25:27,560
No, that's not...

365
00:25:28,530 --> 00:25:32,270
This was an incident that occurred during PE.

366
00:25:32,270 --> 00:25:34,770
Even a dodgeball could...

367
00:25:35,420 --> 00:25:39,020
He threw that ball with malicious intent.

368
00:25:39,570 --> 00:25:42,120
Yes, I cannot deny that.

369
00:25:43,940 --> 00:25:47,560
Excuse me. I am Nashiki, teacher of Class 3.

370
00:25:47,560 --> 00:25:51,210
May I listen in,
as a fellow third grade teacher?

371
00:25:55,070 --> 00:25:59,170
If I may ask, is your daughter still bruised?

372
00:25:59,170 --> 00:26:00,350
Are you doubting us?

373
00:26:00,350 --> 00:26:02,020
No, not at all.

374
00:26:02,740 --> 00:26:07,560
The bruise disappeared the next morning.
However, we have a diagnosis.

375
00:26:07,560 --> 00:26:10,130
[Diagnosis]

376
00:26:10,130 --> 00:26:12,360
What's this?

377
00:26:12,360 --> 00:26:13,930
The bruise is gone, right?

378
00:26:13,930 --> 00:26:15,430
So why all this?

379
00:26:15,430 --> 00:26:17,330
Ms. Nashiki!

380
00:26:17,330 --> 00:26:20,840
Excuse me. I am Ichinose,
a fourth grade teacher.

381
00:26:20,840 --> 00:26:24,640
The middle grades
handle these issues together,

382
00:26:24,640 --> 00:26:27,070
so allow me to listen in as well.

383
00:26:28,130 --> 00:26:29,350
Pardon me.

384
00:26:29,350 --> 00:26:35,470
In any case, we wish to have
Naoya Sano's parents apologize.

385
00:26:35,470 --> 00:26:36,790
Apologize?

386
00:26:36,790 --> 00:26:38,730
Yes. If they refuse,

387
00:26:38,730 --> 00:26:43,850
please tell them I will not hesitate
to bring this to court.

388
00:26:52,470 --> 00:26:57,850
Goodness, all our guardians
are so quick to bring up lawsuits.

389
00:26:57,850 --> 00:27:00,470
Can't they resolve the issue themselves?

390
00:27:00,470 --> 00:27:01,980
Ms. Principal.

391
00:27:04,780 --> 00:27:06,780
I suppose complaining won't help anyone.

392
00:27:06,780 --> 00:27:10,970
We must try to contact Sano's father.

393
00:27:10,970 --> 00:27:12,670
Yes, ma'am.

394
00:27:12,670 --> 00:27:14,290
Mr. Majima.

395
00:27:14,290 --> 00:27:19,820
Your own negligence is to blame
for not contacting him till now.

396
00:27:19,820 --> 00:27:21,840
My apologies.

397
00:27:23,700 --> 00:27:25,430
Ms. Principal.

398
00:27:25,430 --> 00:27:30,320
Sano's father seems to work at night.

399
00:27:31,390 --> 00:27:35,570
But I think he is a kind individual.

400
00:27:35,570 --> 00:27:37,190
<i>You've got rice there.</i>

401
00:27:37,960 --> 00:27:40,460
- <i>Thanks.</i>
- <i>Sure.</i>

402
00:27:40,460 --> 00:27:43,690
I believe he cares for his child.

403
00:27:43,690 --> 00:27:45,990
I'm surprised you know.

404
00:27:45,990 --> 00:27:47,810
Are you acquainted with his father?

405
00:27:47,810 --> 00:27:51,400
No, I...

406
00:27:51,400 --> 00:27:53,550
Naoya told me.

407
00:27:53,550 --> 00:27:55,940
Even though you aren't his teacher?

408
00:27:58,060 --> 00:27:59,950
About that.

409
00:28:01,750 --> 00:28:08,400
Naoya Sano has requested
to join Ms. Nashiki's class.

410
00:28:11,520 --> 00:28:13,360
We will deal with that later.

411
00:28:13,360 --> 00:28:16,310
For now, we must contact his guardian.

412
00:28:16,310 --> 00:28:20,020
Mr. Majima, don't handle this alone, okay?

413
00:28:20,020 --> 00:28:22,290
Yes, ma'am.

414
00:28:22,290 --> 00:28:23,580
We'll be heading out.

415
00:28:23,580 --> 00:28:26,810
- Good night.
- Good night.

416
00:28:35,390 --> 00:28:38,340
Mr. Majima, was everything okay?

417
00:28:38,340 --> 00:28:39,920
Yes.

418
00:28:39,920 --> 00:28:42,430
I'll try calling his father now.

419
00:28:42,430 --> 00:28:46,710
Wait. Write down what you wish to say first.
Otherwise you'll panic.

420
00:28:46,710 --> 00:28:48,380
Right.

421
00:28:50,830 --> 00:28:55,530
7PM... He might be working already.

422
00:28:58,100 --> 00:28:59,430
I'm going to go see him.

423
00:28:59,430 --> 00:29:01,260
Visitations are the homeroom teacher's job.

424
00:29:01,260 --> 00:29:02,760
But I stayed there yesterday.

425
00:29:02,760 --> 00:29:04,160
Huh?

426
00:29:06,150 --> 00:29:08,390
I ate dinner with them, too.

427
00:29:09,180 --> 00:29:10,340
What was that?

428
00:29:10,340 --> 00:29:11,790
I ate egg on rice.

429
00:29:11,790 --> 00:29:13,240
Not what I was asking.

430
00:29:13,240 --> 00:29:15,110
Come with me.

431
00:29:18,110 --> 00:29:19,600
You stayed at their place?

432
00:29:20,120 --> 00:29:23,340
I have to help Naoya, and Master Seki.

433
00:29:23,340 --> 00:29:25,620
"Master Seki"? You're acting weird...

434
00:29:25,620 --> 00:29:28,240
A child wanted to learn.

435
00:29:28,240 --> 00:29:29,830
As a teacher, I can't abandon him.

436
00:29:29,830 --> 00:29:33,070
Teachers now aren't allowed
to get so attached to one student.

437
00:29:33,070 --> 00:29:36,320
- Never?
- Never.

438
00:29:36,320 --> 00:29:39,080
- I see.
- Yeah.

439
00:29:41,510 --> 00:29:44,820
But I'm going anyway.
I promise it'll only be today.

440
00:29:44,820 --> 00:29:47,330
- Tell him about the injury, and...
- Good night.

441
00:29:47,330 --> 00:29:48,640
- Good night.
- Night.

442
00:29:48,640 --> 00:29:49,780
And about Kizaki's parents.

443
00:29:49,780 --> 00:29:51,020
Wait.

444
00:29:51,020 --> 00:29:55,080
If I let you go alone,
things will get more out of hand.

445
00:30:01,680 --> 00:30:04,770
Last night when I visited Naoya's home,

446
00:30:04,770 --> 00:30:09,680
he was getting ready to eat cold rice
with an egg on top for dinner.

447
00:30:10,910 --> 00:30:14,110
He said his mom ran away with another man.

448
00:30:14,110 --> 00:30:21,200
Even so, teachers can't play favorites.
You understand that, right?

449
00:30:21,200 --> 00:30:22,530
Yeah.

450
00:30:23,120 --> 00:30:25,920
You'll make them expect more.

451
00:30:25,920 --> 00:30:27,590
You're right.

452
00:30:27,590 --> 00:30:29,280
Please take one.

453
00:30:30,870 --> 00:30:32,090
Huh?

454
00:30:32,870 --> 00:30:35,280
- Oh.
- What?

455
00:30:35,280 --> 00:30:37,020
This is Naoya's dad.

456
00:30:37,020 --> 00:30:38,830
What?

457
00:30:38,830 --> 00:30:40,490
Ms. Nashiki.

458
00:30:42,880 --> 00:30:45,840
We'd like to resolve this via conversation

459
00:30:45,840 --> 00:30:48,380
before the other party files a lawsuit.

460
00:30:48,950 --> 00:30:51,080
- So tomorrow at 4PM?
- Yes.

461
00:30:51,080 --> 00:30:53,430
Our staff will oversee the exchange as well.

462
00:31:02,860 --> 00:31:05,550
I have to be getting back to work.

463
00:31:14,080 --> 00:31:16,180
Ikuru.

464
00:31:16,180 --> 00:31:17,560
Yeah?

465
00:31:18,340 --> 00:31:20,140
That man...

466
00:31:21,240 --> 00:31:23,400
He looks a lot like Master Seki.

467
00:31:23,400 --> 00:31:25,180
Huh?

468
00:31:25,180 --> 00:31:28,860
But he's got no memory of Master Seki.

469
00:31:28,860 --> 00:31:32,170
He didn't know who I was either.

470
00:31:32,170 --> 00:31:35,040
You told him about you-know-what?

471
00:31:36,790 --> 00:31:40,410
No. He got annoyed
that I kept calling him, "Master Seki".

472
00:31:42,040 --> 00:31:44,300
But the thing is,

473
00:31:44,300 --> 00:31:50,600
I can't help but call him
Master Seki in my heart.

474
00:31:56,950 --> 00:31:59,020
- I'm home.
- Welcome back.

475
00:31:59,570 --> 00:32:01,050
I'm back.

476
00:32:03,660 --> 00:32:05,430
- Iroha!
- Woah!

477
00:32:07,710 --> 00:32:11,170
Why didn't you come home?
I was so worried about you!

478
00:32:11,170 --> 00:32:12,770
Sorry.

479
00:32:12,770 --> 00:32:15,010
I'm sorry, Saya.

480
00:32:16,630 --> 00:32:20,700
Learn how to use a phone already!
I'll teach you.

481
00:32:20,700 --> 00:32:23,180
Could you teach me how to use a tablet, too?

482
00:32:23,180 --> 00:32:27,100
- Of course! So please...
- <i>Why do I have to feel like this?</i>

483
00:32:27,100 --> 00:32:30,090
Don't disappear on us, okay?

484
00:32:30,090 --> 00:32:32,920
<i>Why should I care?</i>

485
00:32:32,920 --> 00:32:37,550
<i>If she has a fated partner, so be it.</i>

486
00:32:38,360 --> 00:32:41,650
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

487
00:32:42,300 --> 00:32:44,500
Ms. Nashiki, Mr. Ichinose.

488
00:32:44,500 --> 00:32:46,210
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

489
00:32:46,210 --> 00:32:48,150
Thank you for helping out yesterday.

490
00:32:48,150 --> 00:32:51,500
We managed to reach out
to the Kizaki's as well.

491
00:32:51,500 --> 00:32:55,800
They said they would also be free today.

492
00:32:55,800 --> 00:32:57,070
- That's great news.
- Yes.

493
00:32:57,070 --> 00:33:01,080
Resolution through conversation
is better than any conflict.

494
00:33:01,080 --> 00:33:04,140
Ms. Nashiki,
could you also join us for the talk?

495
00:33:04,140 --> 00:33:08,670
I think Mr. Sano would feel better
with you there.

496
00:33:08,670 --> 00:33:10,530
- Of course.
- Thank you.

497
00:33:10,530 --> 00:33:17,150
Oh, right. Mrs. Kizaki will be watching us
for our joint PE class today.

498
00:33:17,150 --> 00:33:21,640
I see. Naoya did cause trouble
during gym class.

499
00:33:21,640 --> 00:33:24,110
That's nerve-racking.

500
00:33:24,110 --> 00:33:27,890
If you were planning any ball sports
for class today, even more so.

501
00:33:27,890 --> 00:33:30,040
What's on the the agenda
for third graders today?

502
00:33:35,300 --> 00:33:39,110
Have you all organized yourselves?

503
00:33:39,110 --> 00:33:43,670
We will be practicing our relay race today.

504
00:33:43,670 --> 00:33:46,060
You boys, enough messing around.

505
00:33:46,060 --> 00:33:47,630
Ready,

506
00:33:47,630 --> 00:33:49,370
set...

507
00:33:59,290 --> 00:34:01,050
Ready...

508
00:34:01,050 --> 00:34:02,750
Make sure to stretch!

509
00:34:02,750 --> 00:34:04,520
Kizaki's in first.

510
00:34:04,520 --> 00:34:06,450
Line up here when you're done.

511
00:34:08,810 --> 00:34:10,740
You alright?

512
00:34:10,740 --> 00:34:12,350
Can you stand?

513
00:34:12,350 --> 00:34:14,660
Here, get up.

514
00:34:14,660 --> 00:34:16,320
I'll run with you.

515
00:34:16,320 --> 00:34:17,300
- Really?
- Yeah. Let's go.

516
00:34:17,300 --> 00:34:18,180
Make sure to log your results.

517
00:34:18,180 --> 00:34:20,530
Guys, look! That teacher's running so weird!

518
00:34:20,530 --> 00:34:23,500
- Everyone, settle down.
- Really? I wanna see!

519
00:34:23,500 --> 00:34:24,850
We're in the middle of class.

520
00:34:24,850 --> 00:34:27,180
No way.

521
00:34:28,570 --> 00:34:31,720
- Look at her.
- Weirdo.

522
00:34:33,940 --> 00:34:36,660
Ms. Nashiki, you're running weird!

523
00:34:36,660 --> 00:34:40,050
I am not! My courier buddies
taught me their ways!

524
00:34:40,050 --> 00:34:42,780
Liar!

525
00:34:48,760 --> 00:34:50,190
Ready...

526
00:34:51,240 --> 00:34:54,640
Looking good.

527
00:35:04,320 --> 00:35:06,250
- Miu!
- Mama?

528
00:35:06,250 --> 00:35:08,440
What are you doing?

529
00:35:11,110 --> 00:35:14,100
Mrs. Kizaki, what seems to be the matter?

530
00:35:14,100 --> 00:35:16,480
Mr. Majima, you're pushing my daughter.

531
00:35:16,480 --> 00:35:19,440
- Why are you having her run?
- Huh?

532
00:35:19,440 --> 00:35:22,230
I showed you her diagnosis, no?

533
00:35:22,230 --> 00:35:25,700
Miu is to sit out of PE!

534
00:35:25,700 --> 00:35:27,760
But you did not request...

535
00:35:27,760 --> 00:35:29,580
Mr. Majima.

536
00:35:29,580 --> 00:35:31,810
Are you an idiot?

537
00:35:31,810 --> 00:35:34,760
Do I really have to tell you everything?

538
00:35:34,760 --> 00:35:37,950
Miu, go rest over there, okay?

539
00:35:41,750 --> 00:35:46,610
Where is Naoya Sano?

540
00:35:46,610 --> 00:35:48,870
Ma'am, we are in the middle of class.

541
00:35:48,870 --> 00:35:51,640
I just want to know who he is.

542
00:35:54,160 --> 00:35:56,930
Ma'am, class is currently in session.

543
00:35:56,930 --> 00:36:00,020
If you wish to watch,
please stand over there.

544
00:36:00,920 --> 00:36:02,640
Right this way.

545
00:36:11,860 --> 00:36:13,610
Okay.

546
00:36:14,770 --> 00:36:16,600
Ms. Akutsu.

547
00:36:19,580 --> 00:36:21,710
Thank you.

548
00:36:23,340 --> 00:36:25,100
Pardon me.

549
00:36:34,290 --> 00:36:35,800
Your tea.

550
00:36:38,870 --> 00:36:40,590
[Afterschool club]

551
00:36:40,590 --> 00:36:43,560
You two wait here, alright?

552
00:36:45,040 --> 00:36:48,890
I'm always here after school.

553
00:36:49,580 --> 00:36:51,540
Wanna play cards together?

554
00:36:53,370 --> 00:36:54,300
Okay.

555
00:36:54,300 --> 00:36:57,970
Cool. What do you wanna play?

556
00:37:14,600 --> 00:37:16,910
Yeah. I just got here.

557
00:37:19,190 --> 00:37:21,710
The first floor? I'll be right there.

558
00:37:22,950 --> 00:37:24,540
The Principal's office?

559
00:37:25,440 --> 00:37:28,140
Where on the first floor is that?

560
00:37:28,140 --> 00:37:30,220
Excuse me, Mr. Kizaki?

561
00:37:31,620 --> 00:37:34,530
I am Naoya Sano's father.

562
00:37:36,300 --> 00:37:39,330
We will talk in the office.

563
00:37:39,330 --> 00:37:41,410
Sir, wait.

564
00:37:41,410 --> 00:37:45,220
I will apologize.
I'm sorry for my son's actions.

565
00:37:48,220 --> 00:37:50,510
I do not intend to speak with you directly.

566
00:37:50,510 --> 00:37:51,890
I have merely come for show.

567
00:37:51,890 --> 00:37:55,810
Any further discussions,
you will have with my lawyer.

568
00:37:56,510 --> 00:37:58,410
What?

569
00:38:00,460 --> 00:38:03,150
Hello? Is everything okay?

570
00:38:04,210 --> 00:38:05,490
Dear?

571
00:38:05,490 --> 00:38:08,030
Mrs. Kizaki, wait!

572
00:38:08,030 --> 00:38:09,970
- Is everything okay?
- Mrs. Kizaki.

573
00:38:09,970 --> 00:38:11,910
I apologized, didn't I?

574
00:38:11,910 --> 00:38:13,450
I bowed down to you.

575
00:38:13,450 --> 00:38:15,470
Naoya meant no harm.

576
00:38:15,470 --> 00:38:17,360
He just happened to graze your daughter.

577
00:38:17,360 --> 00:38:19,100
Graze my daughter?

578
00:38:19,100 --> 00:38:21,170
How many days has it been since she was hurt?

579
00:38:21,170 --> 00:38:23,300
Did you even try to contact us?

580
00:38:23,300 --> 00:38:24,940
That's why I'm apologizing now.

581
00:38:24,940 --> 00:38:27,690
It doesn't sound like you're very sorry.

582
00:38:27,690 --> 00:38:29,350
What exactly isn't clicking for you?

583
00:38:29,350 --> 00:38:32,300
I came here because I was asked to apologize.

584
00:38:32,300 --> 00:38:34,130
What else do you need from me?

585
00:38:34,130 --> 00:38:37,480
I've heard enough.
My lawyer will be in touch.

586
00:38:37,480 --> 00:38:39,050
- Money?
- What?

587
00:38:39,050 --> 00:38:43,010
- I am asking for respect...
- And what does that mean to you?

588
00:38:46,060 --> 00:38:48,870
Let us talk this over. Please, follow me.

589
00:38:48,870 --> 00:38:50,930
I have no reason to go.

590
00:38:50,930 --> 00:38:54,270
I didn't realize I was dealing with
such a barbarian.

591
00:38:55,860 --> 00:38:57,900
Did you know?

592
00:38:57,900 --> 00:39:01,110
Children whose parents
do not read aloud to them,

593
00:39:01,110 --> 00:39:04,120
know 30,000 less words than other kids.

594
00:39:04,120 --> 00:39:08,970
They only know to curse,
and cannot speak intellectually.

595
00:39:10,220 --> 00:39:13,420
Pardon me, but where is your son's mother?

596
00:39:15,810 --> 00:39:18,080
Why do you care? I raised Naoya.

597
00:39:18,080 --> 00:39:20,210
Not exactly a harmonious family, no?

598
00:39:20,210 --> 00:39:22,050
I see now.

599
00:39:22,050 --> 00:39:25,500
Yes, I know exactly how your son was raised.

600
00:39:27,250 --> 00:39:29,360
Enough!

601
00:39:30,980 --> 00:39:33,950
I can't let your accusations slide.

602
00:39:33,950 --> 00:39:37,140
Are you saying kids who lack a parent
won't grow into fine adults?

603
00:39:37,140 --> 00:39:38,920
- Ms. Nashiki.
- Don't!

604
00:39:38,920 --> 00:39:42,310
Naoya's at fault for throwing that ball,
I admit that much.

605
00:39:42,310 --> 00:39:45,920
But don't use that
to judge Naoya's character!

606
00:39:45,920 --> 00:39:49,200
What is the deal with this teacher?

607
00:39:49,670 --> 00:39:51,580
I'm not wrong though, am I?

608
00:39:51,580 --> 00:39:53,810
A child takes after their parents.

609
00:39:53,810 --> 00:39:57,880
With a father like him,
how could he turn out decent?

610
00:39:57,880 --> 00:40:00,420
- Bastard...
- Move.

611
00:40:03,210 --> 00:40:07,940
I've heard enough. Quit insulting Naoya!

612
00:40:07,940 --> 00:40:10,450
- Mr. Sano!
- Stop!

613
00:40:18,880 --> 00:40:21,870
Mr. Sano! No violence!

614
00:40:25,440 --> 00:40:26,800
Sorry!

615
00:40:26,800 --> 00:40:28,540
I recorded all of that!

616
00:40:28,540 --> 00:40:31,900
Both parent and teacher are despicable.

617
00:40:32,520 --> 00:40:34,110
Stop it!

618
00:40:37,200 --> 00:40:38,890
Papa...

619
00:40:39,700 --> 00:40:41,340
Mama...

620
00:40:41,340 --> 00:40:43,440
Please, stop.

621
00:40:46,740 --> 00:40:48,790
I'm sorry.

622
00:40:49,750 --> 00:40:52,730
It's not my dad's fault.

623
00:40:52,730 --> 00:40:57,400
I accidentally hit Miu with a ball.

624
00:40:58,850 --> 00:41:00,940
I'm so sorry.

625
00:41:03,990 --> 00:41:07,390
I'm not hurt.

626
00:41:07,390 --> 00:41:08,890
Miu!

627
00:41:08,890 --> 00:41:10,870
You know. Right, Mama?

628
00:41:10,870 --> 00:41:13,160
I'm not bruised.

629
00:41:16,050 --> 00:41:23,070
I just wanted Papa to listen to me.

630
00:41:25,890 --> 00:41:27,530
Miu...

631
00:42:17,590 --> 00:42:19,080
Ms. Nashiki.

632
00:42:19,080 --> 00:42:20,770
Ikuru.

633
00:42:22,540 --> 00:42:24,700
You look tired.

634
00:42:24,700 --> 00:42:26,080
Oh yes.

635
00:42:28,080 --> 00:42:29,790
I'm absolutely beat.

636
00:42:34,950 --> 00:42:36,680
Did you know about these?

637
00:42:36,680 --> 00:42:39,440
Someone placed planters back here.

638
00:42:40,920 --> 00:42:43,970
Yes, I did know.

639
00:42:43,970 --> 00:42:46,660
Ms. Nashiki pointed them out to me before.

640
00:42:50,340 --> 00:42:52,250
I see.

641
00:42:55,760 --> 00:43:01,190
Iroha Nashiki must be a kind soul.

642
00:43:01,190 --> 00:43:05,190
She's nothing like you, that's for sure.

643
00:43:05,190 --> 00:43:06,920
Are you saying I'm not kind?

644
00:43:06,920 --> 00:43:09,080
I never said that.

645
00:43:15,910 --> 00:43:20,630
He really was different.

646
00:43:22,490 --> 00:43:25,310
He really looks exactly like him.

647
00:43:26,080 --> 00:43:28,030
But they're nothing alike.

648
00:43:28,760 --> 00:43:30,880
He's someone entirely different.

649
00:43:33,150 --> 00:43:35,880
I'm such a fool.

650
00:43:35,880 --> 00:43:39,540
Of course Master Seki wouldn't be here.

651
00:43:41,990 --> 00:43:44,460
Everyone here is their own person.

652
00:43:44,460 --> 00:43:49,530
They're all people living their own lives.

653
00:43:56,120 --> 00:44:02,620
Why am I living as someone I'm not?

654
00:44:10,010 --> 00:44:12,010
I want to go home.

655
00:44:18,320 --> 00:44:20,170
I want to go home.

656
00:44:56,180 --> 00:45:00,080
<i>♪ Or do we come to see
Tokubei's wife on the isle? ♪</i>

657
00:45:00,080 --> 00:45:06,180
<i>♪ Three and a four, and a three, and a four ♪</i>

658
00:45:08,010 --> 00:45:09,520
That's our current song.

659
00:45:12,660 --> 00:45:15,900
What a strange tune.

660
00:45:53,920 --> 00:45:56,300
Mr. Ichinose?

661
00:45:56,300 --> 00:45:58,220
What are you doing?

662
00:46:08,620 --> 00:46:13,500
Ms. Nashiki?
